id: mbedtls_entropy_dummy_nvseed
package: security_mbedtls
label: Dummy NV Seed Entropy Source
description: >-
  A very bad implementation of a non-volatile seed for randomness generation in
  Mbed TLS. In fact, this implemention is both predictable and volatile. The
  purpose of this entropy source is to be used before NVM3 and/or a proper TRNG
  is available on S3 devices.
category: Platform|Security|Mbed TLS|Randomness
quality: production
source:
- path: sl_component/sl_mbedtls_support/src/sl_entropy_nvseed_dummy.c
provides:
- name: mbedtls_entropy_source
  allow_multiple: true
- name: mbedtls_entropy_dummy_nvseed
requires:
- name: device_series_3
template_contribution:
- name: mbedtls_config
  value: MBEDTLS_ENTROPY_NV_SEED
- name: mbedtls_config
  value: MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_C
- name: mbedtls_config
  value: MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_NV_SEED_ALT
- name: mbedtls_config
  value: MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_STD_NV_SEED_READ sli_nv_seed_read
- name: mbedtls_config
  value: MBEDTLS_PLATFORM_STD_NV_SEED_WRITE sli_nv_seed_write
root_path: security_mbedtls/platform/security
